# Line-ending policy for mudp.
#
# Go sources and shell scripts must stay LF: `gofmt -l` reports every line of a
# CRLF file as "needs formatting" (the diff is line endings only), and a CRLF
# shebang silently breaks `#!interpreter` exec on Linux. On Windows, where
# core.autocrlf=true is the default, this pins LF on checkout so gofmt, the
# compiler, and shell scripts all see consistent input.
*.go   text eol=lf
*.mod  text eol=lf
*.sum  text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
